            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The present invention relates to a carbonated beverage filling section, which is housed in a sterile chamber, comprising: a convey wheel configured to rotate a plurality of bottles (30); a plurality of filling nozzles arranged along an outer circumference of the convey wheel, each of the filling nozzles being adapted to inject a carbonated beverage inside the bottle; a carbonated beverage supply line connected to the filling nozzles, wherein one end of the carbonated beverage supply line is connected to a filling head tank filled with the sterile carbonated beverage and another end is in communication with the inside of the bottle, so that the sterile carbonated beverage supplied from the filling head tank passes through the carbonated beverage supply line and is injected inside the bottle; a gas supply line connected to the filling nozzles, wherein one end of the gas supply line is connected to the filling head tank and another end is in communication with the inside of the bottle, so that a counter pressure gas supplied from the filling head tank passes through the gas supply line and is filled inside the bottle; and a snift line configured to discharge a gas inside the bottle. The snift line is opened into the carbonated beverage filling device in the sterile chamber. The convey wheel and the filling nozzles are covered with a cover, and a rotary joint is attached to an upper portion of the cover. The rotary joint has a rotating pipe connected to the filling nozzle side and a fixed pipe connected to the filling head tank side. The fixed pipe is a pipe, into which the sterile carbonated beverage from the filling head tank flows. The rotating pipe is a pipe to feed the sterile carbonated beverage from the fixed pipe toward the filling nozzle, and is rotatable together with the convey wheel and the filling nozzle. The fixed pipe and the rotating pipe constitute a portion of the carbonated beverage supply line. A mechanical seal portion is connected to the fixed pipe and the rotating pipe. A boundary surface is formed between the rotating pipe and the fixed pipe of the rotary joint. At the boundary surface, the sterile carbonated beverage flowing inside the fixed pipe and the rotating pipe is sealed with a sterile air in the mechanical seal portion at a temperature of 1°C or more and 40°C or less.</p>
